  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia has ratified six out of eight fundamental conventions. Somalia is the only African country that has not ratified C. 138, and in collaboration with FPRW, promotional ratification activities were organized, including without any concrete indications of making progress toward ratification. 
In 2021, all article 22 reports on fundamental conventions were prepared with the technical assistance of the ILO, but never submitted by the government. First reports of the newly ratified convention were not received, despite several ILO interventions and support activities at all levels. Under aegis of IGAD, additional efforts are made to emphasize the importance of ratification of all 10 fundamental conventions, also with a view to related trade and financing opportunities. urgent request was made to provide technical assistance for a labour law review, taking into account provisions of the seven conventions that were ratified in 2021. 
In view of the situation that Somalia need to ratify Conventions such as C138, and the lack of adequate capacity to submit reports on ratified Conventions, the ILO under CPO SOM826, envisages to ensure that the pending reports are submitted and those to be ratified are considered by the respective government authority.  To this effect, the ILO provides training on ILS reporting to the tripartite constituents. In addition, support will be provided to enhance advocacy efforts of the social partners to ensure that the Conventions tabled for ratifications are actually presented for action.</narrative>
  </description>
